_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1pu[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Task backlog epic 3: publication safety, handoffs, check coverage, [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]and state freshness[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Fix and close the five selected fleet-costly task beads, then [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]continue the backlog chain under the same ranking and closeout [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]rules.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]1[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] wave[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_backlog_epic_3.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/task_backlog_epic_3.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/task_backlog_epic_2.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1pu[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1pu/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Scan and safely recover prompt migrations into the agents [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]sidecar (sase-1os)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]prompt-migration-protection[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt-migration-protection: route the one-time legacy prompt migration [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the shared publication-protection scanner before staging, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stop recommending a raw push after a GH013 rejection. Preserve the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]existing private/quarantine behavior and sanitized diagnostics. Add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regression coverage for clean migration, a detected secret, and a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rejected push; ensure no secret value is emitted or replayed.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Keep long-waiting bead agents alive when their dependency [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]wakes (sase-12v)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]waiter-wake-recovery[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]waiter-wake-recovery: reproduce the wake-time NameCollisionError after a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]long wait, identify the reservation or retry failure, and make the wake [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]path recover or retry safely without launching duplicate successors. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Preserve the original dependency and workspace state. Review the related[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-1el monitor-start report, but do not assume a shared root cause [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from the exception class alone.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Select agent-artifact marker audits for marker-writer changes [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1mv)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]marker-audit-selection[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]marker-audit-selection: make scoped test selection include both AST [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit modules when a changed source file writes a tracked agent-artifact[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]marker, without exceeding the contract-set serial budget or weakening [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the audits. Add selector regression tests and show that a marker-writer [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]change selects both audits.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Remove the full-check timeout for the empty-home SDD identity [bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]test (sase-120)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]sdd-identity-check-flake[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7